    "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 21-layer dielectric multilayer bandpass filter on CaF2 substrate for dual-band transmission. Stack structure from air incident side: Layer 1-6 (Bragg mirror: Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS), Layer 7 (Cavity1 spacer: Ge), Layer 8-13 (Bragg mirror: ZnS/Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS/Ge), Layer 14 (Cavity2 spacer: ZnS), Layer 15-20 (Bragg mirror: Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS), Layer 21 (Cavity3 spacer: Ge), then CaF2 substrate. All 21 layer thicknesses are optimization variables with bounds: 50 nm to 2000 nm. Optimize for: maximize transmittance in 4150-4350 nm band, maximize transmittance in 4550-4750 nm band, minimize transmittance in 3600-4000 nm band, minimize transmittance in 4850-5200 nm band. Normal incidence, air ambient, CaF2 substrate. Use Ge and ZnS as dielectric materials (no metals). Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Design and optimize a 21-layer air|Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS|Ge|ZnS/Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS/Ge|ZnS|Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS/Ge/ZnS|Ge|CaF2 bandpass filter for dual-band transmission in 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm while suppressing transmittance in 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm. Optimize all 21 layer thicknesses between 50 nm and 2000 nm at normal incidence.",
